From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AMD TheRock <noreply@amd.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix swapped SOVERSION/VERSION arguments

set_target_properties()'s VERSION and SOVERSION are swapped: VERSION is
meant to control the full installed filename (libfftw3.so.3.6.9) and
SOVERSION the embedded -soname the dynamic loader actually resolves
against (libfftw3.so.3). Upstream has them backwards, so the linker
embeds "3.6.9" as the SONAME instead of "3".

No distro's own fftw3 package ships a library literally named
libfftw3.so.3.6.9 (they all use libtool's standard libfftw3.so.3), so a
binary linked against this build's fftw3 can never resolve its runtime
dependency against the system-provided library -- the two SONAMEs never
match.

See-also: https://github.com/ROCm/TheRock/pull/8527
See-also: ROCM-30893
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -356,7 +356,7 @@ if (OPENMP_FOUND)
 endif ()
 
 foreach(subtarget ${subtargets})
-  set_target_properties (${subtarget} PROPERTIES SOVERSION 3.6.9 VERSION 3)
+  set_target_properties (${subtarget} PROPERTIES SOVERSION 3 VERSION 3.6.9)
   install (TARGETS ${subtarget}
 	  RUNTIME DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_BINDIR}
 	  LIBRARY DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR}
--
2.43.0

